--[[
	╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
	║              PROTOCOL X HUB — UI LIBRARY  v3.2  (bug-fix release)        ║
	╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
	║  WHAT WAS BROKEN IN v3.1 AND IS FIXED HERE                               ║
	║                                                                          ║
	║   1. CRASH: Instance.new("UIDragDetector") errors on every client/       ║
	║      executor that predates that class, killing the whole script before  ║
	║      the window is shown. Replaced with a manual header drag that works  ║
	║      with mouse AND touch, and no longer fights sliders/toggles.         ║
	║   2. Keybind labels printed "Enum.KeyCode.RightControl" because          ║
	║      FormatKey used type() instead of typeof().                          ║
	║   3. Sliders stacked a NEW UIStroke on both handles on every theme       ║
	║      change (memory + visual artefacts). Strokes are reused now.         ║
	║   4. The active-tab indicator bar was turned ON but never OFF, so every  ║
	║      visited tab kept an accent bar.                                     ║
	║   5. Dropdown / theme popups only closed on MouseButton1 -> on mobile    ║
	║      they could never be dismissed by tapping outside.                   ║
	║   6. Dropdown menu was a clipped Frame: option lists longer than ~6      ║
	║      items were unreachable. It is a ScrollingFrame now, and the         ║
	║      documented `Search = true` option is actually implemented.          ║
	║   7. The outside-click handler for the theme popup was registered twice. ║
	║   8. Notifications: their ScreenGui had no DisplayOrder so they rendered ║
	║      UNDER the window; the close animation tweened Position inside a     ║
	║      UIListLayout (which does nothing); 300px wide off-screen on phones; ║
	║      text was clipped. Rewritten with auto height + fade out.            ║
	║   9. Window size was hard-coded (420x340 / 780x520) and could be bigger  ║
	║      than the actual viewport. Sizing is viewport-relative and re-clamps ║
	║      when the screen rotates/resizes.                                    ║
	║  10. Home page was reachable only once: no way back after opening a tab. ║
	║      There is a Home button in the sidebar now.                          ║
	║  11. Re-running the script stacked GUIs; the floating button could never ║
	║      be re-created after :Destroy(). Old GUIs are cleaned up on load.    ║
	║  12. Theme callbacks were never released and were fired for destroyed    ║
	║      instances; they are pruned now (and errors no longer kill the rest).║
	║  13. Button text used Theme.Main which is invisible on some accents;     ║
	║      text colour is now picked from the accent's luminance.              ║
	║  14. `Reset All` in the Config tab only showed a notification. It now    ║
	║      really restores every component's default value.                    ║
	║  15. Config save/load ignored dropdown/multi values, the theme and the   ║
	║      toggle key, and readfile() was called even when no file existed.    ║
	║  16. Component constructors errored when called without a table          ║
	║      (Tab:Toggle() etc.) and Toggle/Slider never fired the callback for  ║
	║      their default value.                                                ║
	║  17. Floating-button drag never stopped if the finger/mouse was released ║
	║      outside the button, and the 5s hold-to-lock also dragged the button.║
	║  18. Search: results kept the old tab visible, "no results" label was    ║
	║      mis-parented, and descriptions were not searchable.                 ║
	║  19. A saved keybind came back as an empty table (type() sees an         ║
	║      EnumItem as userdata, so it hit the wrong branch) which silently    ║
	║      destroyed the GUI toggle key after Load Config.                     ║
	║  20. Clients without CanvasGroup now fall back to Frame instead of       ║
	║      erroring on GroupTransparency.                                      ║
	║                                                                          ║
	║  API is 100% backwards compatible with v3.1 — additive only.             ║
	╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

